      "writtenOn": "2026-05-15T16:51:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The \"View on Dashboard\" link is one of the most important tools for triaging performance regressions. Perf will automatically filter which benchmarks are affected by a CL; \"View on Dashboard\" graphs the performance of these benchmarks at each merged CL, marking the regressing CL with a red line.\n\nWhen looking at this graph, keep the following in mind:\n- Expand the window range: Considering trend helps determine if the regression is a true change or just a transient spike.\n\n- Look for broad impact: A true regression usually impacts multiple benchmarks.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 142,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 142,
        "endChar": 689
      },
      "fixSuggestions": [
        {
          "fixId": "017d4bae_63895ab5",
          "description": "prompt_to_edit API",
          "replacements": [
            {
              "path": "site/docs/dev/gardening/_index.md",
              "range": {
                "startLine": 142,
                "startChar": 0,
                "endLine": 143,
                "endChar": 0
              },
              "replacement": "5.  The \"View on Dashboard\" link is one of the most important tools for triaging performance regressions. Perf will automatically filter which benchmarks are affected by a CL; \"View on Dashboard\" graphs the performance of these benchmarks at each merged CL, marking the regressing CL with a red line.\n\n    When looking at this graph, keep the following in mind:\n    -   **Expand the window range:** Considering trend helps determine if the regression is a true change or just a transient spike.\n\n    -   **Look for broad impact:** A true regression usually impacts multiple benchmarks.\n\n    The vertical refers to some metric in performance (e.g. seconds) and the horizontal represents time (i.e. CLs). You may click the right hand check boxes to view or hide a line.\n"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "revId": "c0a12b74d8854d70716a9aff75941896be83f407",
